  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Design4Jobs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Levels of poverty are especially high for young, black South Africans with six out of ten facing unemployment. A lack of basic skills in this group makes it even more difficult to move from long term unemployment to employment. Job creating enterprises within South Africa have been established manufacturing products under the fair trade model and distributing predominately to a domestic market. However, with limited access to wider international retailers, the market is limited. A pilot project conducted in 2010 has developed a plan to address this problem. This project aims to scale up the pilot project by: engaging with the expertise of high value retail brands to provide a robust distribution channel and communicate consumer needs to the South African manufacturers; building the capacity of local enterprise, design, manufacturing and marketing organisations to support craft businesses and producers to meet the requirements of the international and local markets; and providing basic skills and enterprise training to unemployed young people seeking to enter the sector. This will increase the knowledge and sales volumes of the micro enterprises, creating more jobs and moving more people out of poverty.</narrative>
  </description>
